Subject: [PATCH 5/5] probe (not for upstream): float64 end to end
 (FP64_PROBE), fp32 probe (FP32_PROBE), step-1 gradient dump, full-precision
 loss / norm log

FP64_PROBE=1: every float cast (.float / .bfloat16 / .half / .to) goes to float64
and the default dtype is float64; KDA runs on Attention Gym's eager oracles
(bound_gate formula, l2norm_fwd_ref, reference_kda + naive_chunk_kda) and the
short convolution as a per-document depthwise conv with the kernel's tap order;
flex attention stays eager (deterministic mode no longer recompiles it); the MoE
experts loop per expert; the chunked loss accumulates in float64.
FP32_PROBE=1: the same casts kept at float32, experts looped, KDA on impl="reference".
GRAD_DUMP=<prefix>: every parameter gradient at step 1, per rank.
REPR_LOG=1: loss and grad norm printed at full precision every step.
